t fold out worse hands that you dominate or build a pot where you are at a positional disadvantage. Checking allows you to see the flop for free and keeps the pot small, which is a prudent strategy for the first hand of the match with a medium-strength hand.\n\nReason: By checking, you take the free opportunity to see the community cards without inflating the pot while being out of position. This minimizes risk while retaining the potential to hit a strong hand on the flop.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
