uld have to fold and lose my equity. Since I am currently leading the overall game, a lower-variance line that preserves chips while maintaining upside is optimal.\n\nReason: I have an Open-Ended Straight Draw but currently only 6-high. Checking gives me a free look at the river to complete my straight. Betting risks a raise which would force me to fold my equity.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
